>> title: Chicken Wings, Air Fryer
>> category: Fried & Crispy
>> tags: chicken, wings, air fryer, basket, snack, weeknight
>> counters: The Air Fryer & the Pot
>> aka: air fryer wings, air fryer chicken wings, basket wings, crispy wings, wings without a fryer
>> servings: 4
>> time: 35 min
>> slack: forgiving — the range is wide because the machines are; a wing that has not gone matt yet goes back in for three minutes and loses nothing
>> washing-up: the basket, the bowl

>> step: Written for a preheated 5.7 L basket. From cold, add three minutes. A 3.5 L basket is two batches, not more minutes.
One basket, one bowl, and the time assumes the basket was hot.

>> step: dry hard, then toss in the bowl you will serve from
Pat @chicken wings{2 1/2%lb}(1.1 kg; split, tips off) dry and toss them in a #bowl{} with @baking powder{1%tsp}, @kosher salt{2%tsp}, @black pepper{1%tsp}.

>> step: roast in the basket 200°C (400°F), 18–24 min, one layer
Roast @&(~1)seasoned wings{} in a preheated #air fryer basket{} at 200°C (400°F) ~air fry{21%min}, one layer with room around each wing.

>> step: turn at halfway — skin gone matt and pebbled, not glossy
Turn @&(~1)wings{} once.

>> step: toss hot in the same bowl
Toss @&(~1)wings{} with @lemon{1%wedge}(juiced over them), @flaky salt{1/2%tsp}.

>> step: A crowded basket steams: one test kitchen lets wings overlap, every other source does not. Give each one room.
Crowded, they steam. The sources disagree about the load, not the clock.
